      "explanationAfterStep": "The cyano group withdraws electrons from boron, so NaBH₃CN is a weaker hydride donor than NaBH₄. It reduces the positive iminium ion fast but leaves the ketone almost untouched, so the ketone, amine and reducing agent can all be mixed at once."
