  "mechanismSummary": "A B–H bond of cyanoborohydride delivers hydride to the carbon of the iminium ion, and the C=N π electrons move onto nitrogen, giving the secondary amine. The ketone is hardly touched: cyanoborohydride is too weak a hydride donor to reduce it at pH 6, so only the iminium ion reacts.",
